    skill_metadata {
      name: "cloudsql-setup"
      description: "Provisions a relational Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL) database and configures Firebase Authentication together. Do NOT use this skill if only Firebase Authentication is requested without a relational database. Do NOT use it for SQLite or other embedded, in-memory, or browser-local databases (sql.js, DuckDB-Wasm, IndexedDB, in-browser SQL over uploaded files) unless a hosted database is also requested.\n\nUse this skill ONLY if the user explicitly requests at least one of:\n* PostgreSQL, Postgres, MySQL, MariaDB, SQL Server, or any other relational SQL database server.\n* SQL, an RDBMS, or a relational database for persisting app data.\n* Cloud SQL, Supabase, Neon, RDS, Aurora, or a similar hosted SQL database service.\n* SQL tooling such as Drizzle, Prisma, pgvector, or another SQL ORM, query builder, or PostgreSQL extension.\n\nCapabilities of the provisioned Cloud SQL instance with Developer edition:\n* Near-instant provisioning (~2 seconds).\n* Scale-to-zero capabilities with a free tier for cost savings."
    }
    line_range_bytes: 35632
  }
