    thinking: "**Analyzing the Cloud Setup**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the nuances of the cloud setup requirements in relation to the frontend and data visualization specifics. The distinction between `cloudsql-setup` and the explicit stack components is crucial, so I\'m cross-referencing to ensure alignment. This analysis will guide the solution architecture, particularly regarding how data flows.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Integration**\n\nI\'m now investigating the Supabase setup, specifically the use of PostgreSQL for relational data, including aggregate statistics and real-time user rankings. The key is understanding how the mock data will integrate with the Supabase Realtime and Auth features within this relational database. I\'m focusing on the expected deliverables - the database schema, frontend architecture, and the implementation of specific screens. The mock data will really drive how I set up the database and frontend.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating SQL Needs**\n\nI\'m revisiting the use of `cloudsql-setup`. The trigger rules now seem questionable. I\'m carefully reassessing whether the user explicitly requested a hosted SQL database. It\'s a key distinction. I must clarify if interactive tools are the standard path and how a manual fallback would impact the implementation. My aim is to make sure this is the right approach.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now carefully dissecting the prompt. My focus is understanding its implied requirements. I\'m noting the phrasing around the expected deliverables, particularly the SQL schema and how it relates to Supabase and PostgreSQL. I\'m evaluating the potential need to call `CheckFeatureEligibility` and determining whether a `cloudsql_setup` UI should trigger a pause in the process. I have to figure out if this is a single turn evaluation, or interactive.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Immediate Demo**\n\nNow I\'m completely focused on Deliverable #3 and its call for an immediate demonstration using realistic mocked data in the frontend. The complete SQL schema is a critical component too, especially `percentile_cont(0.5)` and optimized indexes. The prompt seems to prioritize getting a runnable demo to the user immediately, so delaying that for a Cloud SQL setup dialog is the wrong move. The demo\'s realistic mock data will directly inform the Supabase database schema and guide the frontend architecture. I now fully understand that.\n\n\n**Reframing Deliverables Focus**\n\nI now see clearly that enforcing Firebase Auth and Cloud SQL setup before showing mocked data goes against the prompt\'s intent for an immediate demonstration. The suggested \"Stack Tecnol\303\263gica\" uses Supabase (PostgreSQL), which is different from a requirement. The prompt prioritizes \"demonstra\303\247\303\243o imediata\" with mocked data, making the database schema and frontend the key focus. I\'m now certain I must focus on delivering the mock data demo first.\n\n\n**Confirming Prompt Priority**\n\nNow, I\'m absolutely certain about the immediate priority: a fully interactive frontend application using realistic Brazilian Medical Residency mock data, with local storage for user progress and preferences, and the complete PostgreSQL schema (with optimized indexes and `percentile_cont(0.5)` materialized views/queries). I understand that a `cloudsql-setup` call is inappropriate. I\'m focusing on providing the user with an immediately usable demo. I\'m now reviewing the `frontend-design` files.\n\n\n"
