  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the R1Med Platform**\n\nI\'m incredibly energized by the clarity of the initial concept! This architectural blueprint is fantastic. I\'m focusing on designing a market-leading Brazilian Medical Residency Question Bank platform. Considering MedPulse or R1Med for the name. It needs to be truly standout.\n\n\n**Refining the Branding**\n\nI\'ve got the name, MedR1, and I\'m really pleased with it. It\'s clean and sounds medical and Brazilian! Now I\'m focusing on the brand identity. I\'ve chosen Plus Jakarta Sans for the UI and headings and DM Sans for the body text, and am looking at JetBrains Mono with tabular-nums for data. The dual light and dark themes are also defined! The primary accent color is decided as a deep Clinical Teal/Cyan-Blue.\n\n\n**Defining Semantic Data Colors**\n\nI\'ve nailed down the semantic data color palette! I\'ve gone with Emerald for \"Correto,\" Amber for \"Aten\303\247\303\243o,\" and Crimson for \"Errado,\" ensuring a clear visual distinction. Dark mode variants are also incorporated. I\'m focusing on ensuring these colors are always paired with explicit labels and icons to avoid any ambiguity. Also, I\'ve got the `@custom-variant` tweak to support dark mode consistently.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive Clinical Image Lightbox with zoom and pan controls directly into the question stems. I\'m imagining how great it will look with both X-ray and CT scan examples, along with the correct diagnostic information. Also I\'ve installed `recharts`, `clsx`, and `tailwind-merge` to build some clean, interactive charts.\n\n\n**Optimizing Image Generation**\n\nI\'m now coordinating concurrent tasks: image generation with `generate_image`, and applet package installation. My focus is ensuring Phase 1 image generation completes before moving to Phase 2. I\'m also preparing to carefully plan the sections and modules of the system before executing the Phase 1 tools. Finally, I\'ve got to plan for the database deliverables, and how they may be inspected.\n\n\n**Defining the Database**\n\nI\'ve decided against a Prisma schema in favor of a clean UI for students. Instead, I\'ll create `/database/schema.sql` and `/database/schema.prisma` with a focus on a comprehensive PostgreSQL DDL. This will include hierarchical taxonomy tables, the critical tables, composite indexes, and materialized views with SQL functions for community median/P75 accuracy. I\'ll outline this in the final report, too.\n\nI\'m now focusing on core application views, ensuring they are interactive and in Portuguese. I\'m building out a Sidebar Navigation and Contextual Top Bar.\n\n\n**Designing the Application**\n\nI\'m structuring the application views. The top bar will be clean, with a breadcrumb/view title on the left and minimal controls on the right (Focus Mode toggle, Dark/Light Theme toggle, Profile shortcut). When \"Modo Foco\" is activated during Question Solving or Exam Simulation, the sidebar and ranking widget will collapse for a zero-distraction exam environment. I\'m focusing on these four main modules: Banco de Quest\303\265es, Desempenho & Mediana, Simulado, and Caderno.\n\n\n**Developing the Ranking System**\n\nI\'m now integrating a dynamic, real-time live ranking system! It will showcase the top 10+ students online, with activity indicators and a weighted score formula. I\'m focusing on features such as instant pseudonymous/anonymous mode with a custom nickname and a random medical codename generator. I\'m also planning a temporal evolution line chart comparing student progress against the community median.\n\n\n\n**Expanding the Question Bank**\n\nI\'m now focusing on curating authentic Brazilian residency questions across all five major areas. I\'m adding realistic examples for each field, complete with relevant data tables and images. I\'m prioritizing questions from respected institutions, and building an accessible question bank.\n\n\n**Adding Question Details**\n\nI\'m deep in the specifics of the question bank now. I\'m adding realistic examples for Cirurgia Geral, Ginecologia e Obstetr\303\255cia, and Pediatria. I\'m focusing on providing details like exam sources, relevant tables, and image generation specifications for each new entry.\n\n\n**Expanding the Question Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating 16 deeply realistic questions into the bank, focusing on Medicina Preventiva e Social. Each will feature full clinical vignettes and optional structured lab tables, including one outdated and one annulled question to test the filtering capabilities. I\'m focusing on ensuring data accuracy.\n\n\n**Refining Question Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the finer details of each question\'s structure. I\'m focusing on incorporating high-res clinical images with zoom, 4 or 5 alternatives, and realistic community distribution percentages with a principal distractor and global accuracy. I\'ll also ensure dynamically computed difficulty levels, a comprehensive commentary, and authentic references are included.\n\n\n**Defining Question Filter Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing dynamic, interactive filtering for the question bank. I\'m focusing on features such as live counter updates and boolean filter toggles. Study and Exam Simulation modes will have instant feedback, revealing global accuracy and animated community distribution bars. I\'m building out a didactic commentary for more in-depth learning.\n\n\n**Developing Exam Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating a fully configurable exam simulation mode with a countdown timer, pause/resume functionality, and an interactive question navigator strip. I\'m focusing on providing students with the ability to strike through options, mark questions for review, and access detailed post-exam summaries with community performance comparisons.\n\n\n**Synchronizing User Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating real-time synchronization between study and simulated exam modes. Completed questions immediately update performance charts and the live ranking. Missed questions and bookmarked ones are automatically added to an error notebook. I\'m focusing on ensuring this seamless user experience across different modules.\n\n\n\n"
