  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Medical Authenticity**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased with the latest output! The three clinical images generated are astoundingly realistic and medically accurate. Specifically, the anterior STEMI ECG is textbook perfect, displaying massive ST elevation in V2-V3. It truly captures the essence of a real-world clinical scenario.\n\n\n**Implementing Project Architecture**\n\nI\'ve made considerable progress on project architecture. I\'m focusing on a modular and scalable React + TypeScript + Shadcn-style UI, ensuring it aligns precisely with Deliverable #2. I\'m finalizing the database schemas, including PostgreSQL/Supabase DDL with composite indexes and RLS policies. The Prisma schema mirrors the medical taxonomy and analytics tables.\n\n\n**Defining UI Foundation**\n\nI\'m solidifying the UI foundation with Google Fonts integration. I\'ve added Jakarta Sans, DM Sans, and JetBrains Mono, syncing the MedR1 meta/title. I\'ve built the index.css file with Tailwind v4, custom dark variants, and clinical design tokens, implementing tabular numerals. I\'m focusing on crafting a strong data layer and domain models.\n\n\n**Constructing Component Library**\n\nMy attention is now on building out the component library. I am leveraging Shadcn\'s approach, crafting crisp UI elements. I\'ve been focusing on `Button`, `Select`, and `Switch` components. I\'m also developing the `Sidebar` and `TopBar` layouts and building a real-time, combinable `FilterPanel` to enhance question exploration. I\'m also implementing the `ClinicalImageViewer` component.\n\n\n**Developing UI Modules**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the UI modules. I\'m building out core components, including `QuestionCard.tsx` for both Study and Simulado modes, incorporating features like strikethrough, doubt flags, and community options. I\'m simultaneously working on the `SimuladoBar.tsx` component, which includes the countdown timer, question navigation, and post-exam result summary.\n\n\n"
