  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining UI Structure**\n\nI\'m focused on the UI architecture, leaning heavily on the `frontend-design` principles established earlier. The clean, single-elevation surface is paramount. No static pills, tabular numerals are used. Explicit icon+text semantic states are also crucial. Keyboard accessibility and light/dark mode paired classes are the focus. I am ensuring there are no thick left borders in the layout.\n\n\n**Defining Flashcard Specs**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the detailed requirements for the `localStorage`-backed SRS flashcard feature. The aim is Anki-level quality. I\'m focusing on the navigation; a \"Flashcards\" item with a due-today count is paramount. Filters by specialty and subject will be right within the Flashcards view.\n\n\n**Implementing Flashcard Actions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Gerar Flashcards dos Erros\" action button, providing a quick way to create flashcards from missed questions, plus an optional \"Auto-criar flashcards ao errar\" switch. I\'m also adding a per-row button on each Error Notebook item to create or display its flashcard status. I\'m building a simple, comprehensive SRS flashcard review screen, with 5 pre-seeded flashcards. The front of each card will have a clinical question with metadata, and a \"Virar card\" button with Spacebar shortcut is on deck.\n\n\n**Designing Review Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the SRS flashcard review screen, and how the user will interact with it. The UI now features the **P\303\251rola Cl\303\255nica / Ponto-Chave** concisely. The answer is presented, and includes a link to open the original question. Crucially, I\'m integrating four SRS evaluation buttons with both clickability and keyboard shortcuts. They\'ll be labelled with both textual cues and due date previews. I\'m carefully implementing the SRS algorithms with SM-2, adapting intervals based on ease factor and repetitions, so new/first review cards are shown in the format specified.\n\n\n**Expanding Flashcard Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating custom flashcard creation, handling the full deck list display, and adding deletion/reset options. Crucially, I\'m integrating the exact current interval calculation display on each button, and ensuring all data persists correctly. I\'m also carefully defining the data types and files involved, and making these modifications: Add `flashcards` to `ActiveTab`, define `Flashcard`, `SrsRating`, `FlashcardSource`, plus defining a dedicated SRS algorithm module to enable new functionalities. I am also implementing 5 new realistic initial clinical flashcards.\n\n\n**Implementing Feature Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the core flashcard functionalities: From `recordAnswer` I\'m implementing auto-creation, with hooks on `recordBatchAnswers`, using `FlashcardFromQuestion`, and `generateFlashcardsFromErrors` to create. The review process is encapsulated by `reviewFlashcard`, including custom flashcard actions such as create, delete, and calculating the due card count. I\'ve finished the `FlashcardsView.tsx` with metrics, filtering, and study stage with keyboard shortcuts. I\'m adding an empty state and deck manager table, as well as a new flashcard quick form. I\'m also updating Sidebar and TopBar.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "tygCa9LtO7y0kdUP2L346AI"
