  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the examSearch field**\n\nI\'m imagining a super intelligent `examSearch` field, within `QuestionFilters`. This is specifically designed for Brazilian residency queries. I\'m focusing on making it clean and intuitive.\n\n\n**Refining search term handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the `examSearch` field will handle various user inputs, like `\"ENARE 2025\"` or `\"USP 2025\"`. I\'ve realized that the tokenization and normalization must be robust. Every token provided by the user needs to be present in the normalized exam identity string, which includes `instituicao`, `ano`, `banca`, `tipoProva`, and a code. I\'m considering edge cases.\n\n\n**Implementing autocomplete suggestions**\n\nI\'m now thinking about providing real-time autocomplete suggestions to the user. I envision attaching an HTML `<datalist>` populated with unique `\"instituicao ano\"` exams from `MEDICAL_QUESTIONS`. I\'ll sort them with the newest first to help users, for example, search for `\"ENARE 2025\"`, `\"USP 2025\"`. The exam search will be a side-by-side text input within `FilterPanel`, with a relevant icon. I\'ll also include `filters.examSearch.trim()` in `activeFilterCount`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "0CsCa-HZLKzpz7IPpbHAwQI"
