  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **MedR1 \342\200\224 Banco de Quest\303\265es para Resid\303\252ncia M\303\251dica (Brasil)** (React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS v4 + Recharts + `localStorage` persistence).\n- **Previously Completed Turns (all verified passing `compile_applet` + `lint_applet`)**:\n  - Full MedR1 app with Question Bank, Study/Simulado modes, Clinical Image PACS viewer, Analytics Dashboard, Live Ranking, Error Notebook, Specific-Exam Search (`examSearch` in `FilterPanel`), FSRS-4.5 Flashcards with Forecast Widget & Hover/Focus Tooltips, Dynamic & Individualized FSRS Retention (`calculateDynamicRetention` in `src/lib/srs.ts` + `src/lib/examWeights.ts`), Interactive Exam Incidence Matrix Modal (`src/components/flashcards/ExamWeightsModal.tsx` persisted in `medr1_custom_exam_weights`), and Dynamic 80/20 Pareto Calculator (`src/lib/paretoCalculator.ts`).\n- **Current Active User Request**:\n  - Add a **Combined Pareto (80/20) Chart** to the **Desempenho** (`PerformanceDashboard`) tab:\n    1. Create `src/components/analytics/ParetoChart.tsx` using Recharts (`ComposedChart` with `Bar`, `Line`, and `ReferenceLine`) connected to `calculateExamPareto` in `src/lib/paretoCalculator.ts`:\n       - Quick board/exam selector (`UEPA`, `ENARE`, `Geral`) in the card header.\n       - Left Y-axis: topic incidence bars (%) for the selected board; Right Y-axis: cumulative Pareto curve (`0%` to `100%`).\n       - Dashed horizontal `ReferenceLine` at `80%` labeled `\'Corte Pareto 80%\'`.\n       - Visually highlight Pareto Core bars (up to 80%) in distinct crimson/red when individual student accuracy on that topic is `< 70%` (`\'Gargalo de Alta Incid\303\252ncia\'`), sky blue when `>= 70%`, and muted slate outside the 80% core.\n       - Detailed custom tooltip showing: Tema, Incid\303\252ncia na Banca (%), Acumulado Pareto (%), and Taxa de Acerto Individual do Aluno (%).\n    2. Integrate `<ParetoChart />` into the **Desempenho / Analytics** tab (`PerformanceDashboard.tsx`), accompanied by a quick summary listing the **\'Top 3 Temas de Maior ROI\'** (high incidence in the board + lowest individual student accuracy) with buttons to filter **Quest\303\265es** or **Flashcards** for those topics.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed in Current Turn (NOT YET VERIFIED by `compile_applet` / `lint_applet`)\n1. `/src/lib/paretoCalculator.ts`:\n   - Added and exported `calculateExamPareto = calculateParetoByExam` alias right after `calculateParetoByExam` so callers can import `calculateExamPareto` directly.\n2. `/src/components/analytics/ParetoChart.tsx`:\n   - Created complete component using Recharts (`ResponsiveContainer`, `ComposedChart`, `Bar`, `Cell`, `Line`, `XAxis`, `YAxis`, `CartesianGrid`, `Tooltip`, `ReferenceLine`).\n   - Connected directly to `calculateExamPareto`, `buildBoardParetoProfile`, `getEffectiveBoardTopics`, and `BOARD_INCIDENCE_MATRIX`.\n   - Includes quick board selector (`UEPA`, `ENARE`, `Geral`), semantic color legend, left/right dual Y-axes, dashed amber `ReferenceLine` at `y={80}` (`Corte Pareto 80%`), bottleneck highlighting (`isParetoCore && studentAccuracyPct < 70` -> crimson `#DC2626`/`#F87171`), detailed `ParetoTooltip` (Tema, Incid\303\252ncia na Banca %, Acumulado Pareto %, Acerto Individual %), and the **Top 3 Temas de Maior ROI** 3-column summary strip with `Quest\303\265es` and `Flashcards` filter buttons.\n   - Props interface:\n     ```ts\n     interface ParetoChartProps {\n       initialBoard: ExamBoard;\n       topicRows: PerformanceRow[];\n       areaRows: PerformanceRow[];\n       darkMode: boolean;\n       onFilterQuestionsByTopic: (payload: {\n         topicLabel: string;\n         matchedTema?: string;\n         grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId;\n       }) => void;\n       onFilterFlashcardsByTopic: (payload: {\n         topicLabel: string;\n         matchedTema?: string;\n         grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId;\n       }) => void;\n     }\n     ```\n\n### Remaining (Not Yet Edited)\n1. `/src/components/analytics/PerformanceDashboard.tsx`: Needs to accept `targetBoard`, `onFilterQuestionsByTopic`, `onFilterFlashcardsByTopic` and render `<ParetoChart />`.\n2. `/src/components/flashcards/FlashcardsView.tsx`: Needs an optional `externalFilter?: { grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId; tema?: string; token: number } | null` prop + `useEffect` so clicking \"Flashcards\" on a Top-3 ROI topic jumps to the Flashcards tab pre-filtered to that area/topic (with fallback to `all` area / `\'\'` tema if no exact tema exists in the user\'s current deck, or matching area so the view isn\'t empty!).\n3. `/src/App.tsx`: Needs to wire `targetBoard={store.targetBoard}`, `onFilterQuestionsByTopic`, and `onFilterFlashcardsByTopic` into `<PerformanceDashboard />` and pass `externalFilter` into `<FlashcardsView />`.\n4. Final build + lint verification (`compile_applet` + `lint_applet` in parallel).\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Topic Matching Across Bank & Flashcards**:\n  - Matrix topic labels (e.g., `\"Trauma e Abdome Agudo\"`, `\"Pr\303\251-Natal e Alto Risco\"`, `\"Anticoncep\303\247\303\243o e SUA\"`) are already resolved in `ParetoChart.tsx` into `matchedTema` (matching `HISTORICAL_TOPIC_PERFORMANCE` / `MEDICAL_QUESTIONS`, e.g., `\"Abdome Agudo\"`, `\"Obstetr\303\255cia / Pr\303\251-Natal\"`, `\"Ginecologia\"`) and `grandeAreaId`.\n  - When routing to **Quest\303\265es** (`onFilterQuestionsByTopic`), set `filters` to `{ ...DEFAULT_FILTERS, grandeAreaId: grandeAreaId ?? \'\', tema: exactBankTema ?? \'\', search: exactBankTema ? \'\' : fallbackKeyword, excluirAnuladasDesatualizadas: false }` (checking if `matchedTema` exists in `MEDICAL_QUESTIONS`; if not, fallback to `grandeAreaId` or `search` so the user never lands on an empty result set).\n  - When routing to **Flashcards** (`onFilterFlashcardsByTopic`), pass `{ grandeAreaId, tema: matchedTema, token: Date.now() }` to `FlashcardsView`. Inside `FlashcardsView`, check whether any flashcard exists for `tema`; if yes, set `selectedArea` to `grandeAreaId` (or `\'all\'`) and `selectedTema` to `tema`; if no card matches `tema` yet, filter by `grandeAreaId` (and switch `practiceAhead` or `viewMode` cleanly if all cards in that area are scheduled for later, or stay in `revisao` where the user can click \"Revisar adiantado\" / switch to `baralho`).\n- **No Circular Imports**: `paretoCalculator.ts` only imports types from `examWeights.ts`, so `examWeights.ts` and `ParetoChart.tsx` import runtime functions from `paretoCalculator.ts` cleanly.\n- **Recharts TypeScript Types**: Always guard Tooltip `formatter` values or use custom Tooltip components (`ParetoTooltip` already uses custom JSX component with typed payload, avoiding Recharts v3 `ValueType | undefined` issues).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- No errors encountered in the current turn yet (build/lint not yet run for `ParetoChart.tsx`).\n- Prior turns verified clean with zero errors on `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- `ParetoChart.tsx` is fully written and ready to be mounted inside `PerformanceDashboard.tsx`.\n- In `PerformanceDashboard.tsx`, `PerformanceRow` is already exported (line 31) and imported by `ParetoChart.tsx`.\n- `PerformanceDashboard.tsx` currently has:\n  - Top 4-column KPI strip (lines 166\342\200\223226)\n  - Charts Row (`Aluno vs. Mediana` + `Evolu\303\247\303\243o Temporal`, lines 228\342\200\223526)\n  - Sortable Detailed Analytical Table (lines 528\342\200\223697)\n  - Best placement for `<ParetoChart />`: right between the **Charts Row** and the **Sortable Detailed Analytical Table** (full width so the 12-bar dual-axis ComposedChart and the 3-column Top 3 ROI strip have generous horizontal breathing room!).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Update `/src/components/analytics/PerformanceDashboard.tsx`**:\n   - Import `ExamBoard` from `../../types/medical` and `ParetoChart` from `./ParetoChart`.\n   - Extend `PerformanceDashboardProps` with:\n     - `targetBoard: ExamBoard`\n     - `onFilterQuestionsByTopic: (payload: { topicLabel: string; matchedTema?: string; grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId }) => void`\n     - `onFilterFlashcardsByTopic: (payload: { topicLabel: string; matchedTema?: string; grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId }) => void`\n   - Render `<ParetoChart initialBoard={targetBoard} topicRows={analytics.topicRows} areaRows={analytics.areaRows} darkMode={darkMode} onFilterQuestionsByTopic={onFilterQuestionsByTopic} onFilterFlashcardsByTopic={onFilterFlashcardsByTopic} />` between the Charts Row and the Detailed Analytical Table.\n2. **Update `/src/components/flashcards/FlashcardsView.tsx`**:\n   - Add optional prop `externalFilter?: { grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId; tema?: string; token: number } | null`.\n   - Add a `useEffect` watching `externalFilter?.token`: when set, resolve whether `flashcards` contains cards matching `externalFilter.tema`; if so, set `selectedArea(externalFilter.grandeAreaId ?? \'all\')` and `selectedTema(externalFilter.tema)`; else if cards exist for `externalFilter.grandeAreaId`, set `selectedArea(externalFilter.grandeAreaId)` and `selectedTema(\'\')`; reset `sessionIndex(0)` and switch to `viewMode(\'baralho\')` if zero cards are due today in that filter (or stay in `\'revisao\'` if due cards exist) so the user immediately sees matching flashcards!\n3. **Update `/src/App.tsx`**:\n   - Add `flashcardExternalFilter` state (`{ grandeAreaId?: GrandeAreaId; tema?: string; token: number } | null`).\n   - Implement `handleFilterQuestionsFromPareto` (filters `MEDICAL_QUESTIONS` smartly by `matchedTema` or `grandeAreaId`/`search`, switches to `questoes` in `estudo` mode, resets `currentIndex` to `0`) and `handleFilterFlashcardsFromPareto` (sets `flashcardExternalFilter` with new `Date.now()` token and switches `activeTab` to `\'flashcards\'`).\n   - Pass `targetBoard={store.targetBoard}`, `onFilterQuestionsByTopic={handleFilterQuestionsFromPareto}`, and `onFilterFlashcardsByTopic={handleFilterFlashcardsFromPareto}` to `<PerformanceDashboard />`, and `externalFilter={flashcardExternalFilter}` to `<FlashcardsView />`.\n4. **Final Verification**:\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in parallel. Fix any TypeScript/build issues if any arise and re-verify.\n5. **Respond to User**:\n   - Provide a concise, scannable Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR`) summary covering the new Combined Pareto (80/20) chart, bottleneck highlighting (`<70%` inside the 80% Pareto Core), detailed tooltip, and Top 3 ROI topics with one-click filtering to Questions and Flashcards.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Language**: Respond in Brazilian Portuguese (`pt-BR`).\n- **Design Constitution**: Zero static pill boxes on metadata, single-elevation hairline borders, tabular numerals (`tabular-nums`), accessible controls, full Light/Dark mode parity.\n- **Communication Style**: Concise, scannable completion summary without hype or raw file paths.\n- **Verification**: Always co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together on the final build check before concluding the turn.\n</summary>"
