  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Retention Estimates**\n\nI\'m working on `estimateDaysToTargetRetention` in `src/lib/srs.ts`. I\'ve defined `HighIncidenceRetentionProjection` with `targetRetentionPct`, `estimatedDays` (nullable), and `reached` properties. I aim for a clean and transparent implementation to track retention effectively.\n\n\n**Analyzing Accuracy Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on calculating `accuracyPct`. For high-incidence topics, I\'m gathering accuracy metrics for each flashcard with questions, using `lookupTopicMetric`. I\'m carefully considering how to weight this to reflect current student performance in key areas, hoping to integrate both the weighted average current retention and the SRS pass rate for today. I\'m also ensuring that empty results gracefully handle cases where no topics are high-incidence, returning `null` for `estimatedDays`.\n\n\n**Calculating Daily Cadence**\n\nI\'m now determining `dailyCadence`. I\'m calculating `recentWeeklyCards`, considering cards reviewed in the last 7 days and any recent card repetitions. I\'m looking at active reviews today (`reviewsTodayStats.total`) to estimate `historicalDaily`, by using a base of `recentLast7dCount / 3`, if today\'s reviews are absent. Finally, I\'ll calculate `dailyCadence`, balancing current review stats and history, by blending in `totalReps`.\n\n\n**Determining Daily Cadence**\n\nI\'ve finalized the daily cadence logic. I\'ve considered several factors: current reviews, recent activity, and historical trends. The cadence adapts dynamically. For example, if there\'s no recent activity, I use a base of six. If reviews are present, the calculation blends recent weekly card counts with a weighted historical daily estimate, and uses `totalReps`. I also determine if the cadence is estimated or not.\n\n**Assessing Card Consolidation**\n\nI\'m now determining current retention for high-incidence cards. I am considering card consolidation, stability and retrievability, using FSRS 4.5 criteria. A reliable 95% steady-state retention is reached once `stability >= 12` days, and retrievability is high, or with greater stability for 7 day cycles. For new cards, a topic accuracy is used with an adjusted range. I will determine if each card is consolidated.\n\n\n**Calculating Review Passes**\n\nI\'m now calculating the review passes required for high-incidence cards to reach 95% stability. I\'ve broken down passes needed based on card states (Consolidated, Review, Learning, New). I sum the base passes and adjust by an accuracy multiplier using an accuracy friction factor, which increases passes needed with lower accuracy. I\'m computing the calendar days needed by considering the cadence workload, scaling for the high-incidence card share of the deck.\n\n\n**Estimating Days to Target**\n\nI\'m now integrating the FSRS spacing logic into the `estimatedDays` calculation. I\'ve considered that even with a high daily review count, consolidating new cards takes calendar time due to the spacing intervals. I\'ve computed `spacingFloorDays` based on the retention gap. Finally, I\'ve integrated this into a new formula to estimate total days needed, now including a clamping upper bound.\n\n\n**Integrating Compact Card**\n\nI\'ve determined that the `estimatedDays` is approximately 11, considering workload and spacing, though it will decrease in real-time as reviews increase stability, and passes rise. Any change in Banca-Alvo or ExamWeightModal triggers an immediate recalculation. I am also currently working on the visual design, considering placement of a compact card at the top of the `FlashcardsView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Compact Card**\n\nI\'m focusing on the visual design and placement of the compact card. I\'m aiming for a clean, unmistakable single-row display at the top of `FlashcardsView`. It will feature a progress bar reflecting current retention, the estimated days to target, and key metadata like the active exam and the number of consolidated high-incidence cards. Specifically, I\'m considering using inline text for clarity and a subtle sky/emerald progress bar, with key metrics in bold.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "0DQCa7uROuqv_PUPzqatyAg"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11207526740060072395"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add estimateDaysToTargetRetention helper to compute FSRS-grounded days to 95% retention on high-incidence topics\", \"EndLine\":655, \"Instruction\":\"Add HighIncidenceRetentionProjection interface and estimateDaysToTargetRetention function right after getCardCurrentRetrievabilityPct in src/lib/srs.ts.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function getCardCurrentRetrievabilityPct(\\n  card: Flashcard,\\n  now: Date = new Date()\\n): number | null {\\n  if (card.state === \'New\' || card.stability <= 0) return null;\\n  const elapsed = computeElapsedDays(card, now);\\n  return Math.round(computeRetrievability(elapsed, card.stability) * 100);\\n}\\n\\nexport interface HighIncidenceRetentionProjection {\\n  targetRetentionPct: number;\\n  estimatedDays: number | null;\\n  reachedTarget: boolean;\\n  highIncidenceCount: number;\\n  consolidatedCount: number;\\n  currentRetentionPct: number;\\n  accuracyPct: number;\\n  dailyCadence: number;\\n  isCadenceEstimated: boolean;\\n  board: ExamBoard;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Estimates how many calendar days are required to reach `targetRetentionPct` (default 95%)\\n * across high-incidence topics for the selected exam board, combining:\\n * - Current FSRS stability/retrievability of high-incidence flashcards\\n * - Individual accuracy rate across high-incidence topics (questions + today\'s SRS pass rate)\\n * - Observed daily review cadence (reviews/day)\\n */\\nexport function estimateDaysToTargetRetention(\\n  flashcards: Flashcard[],\\n  selectedBoard: ExamBoard,\\n  userAccuracyByTopic: Record<string, number>,\\n  reviewsTodayStats: { date: string; total: number; passed: number },\\n  targetRetentionPct: number = 95,\\n  now: Date = new Date()\\n): HighIncidenceRetentionProjection {\\n  const highIncidenceCards = flashcards.filter(\\n    (fc) =>\\n      getExamTopicWeight(selectedBoard, fc.tema, fc.subtema, fc.front).tier === \'alta\'\\n  );\\n\\n  if (highIncidenceCards.length === 0) {\\n    return {\\n      targetRetentionPct,\\n      estimatedDays: null,\\n      reachedTarget: false,\\n      highIncidenceCount: 0,\\n      consolidatedCount: 0,\\n      currentRetentionPct: 0,\\n      accuracyPct: 0,\\n      dailyCadence: reviewsTodayStats.total > 0 ? reviewsTodayStats.total : 6,\\n      isCadenceEstimated: reviewsTodayStats.total === 0,\\n      board: selectedBoard,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // 1. Resolve individual accuracy rate across high-incidence topics\\n  const topicAccuracies: number[] = [];\\n  for (const fc of highIncidenceCards) {\\n    const rawAcc = lookupTopicMetric(userAccuracyByTopic, fc);\\n    if (rawAcc !== null) {\\n      const normalized = rawAcc <= 1 && rawAcc >= 0 ? rawAcc * 100 : rawAcc;\\n      topicAccuracies.push(normalized);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  const avgQuestionAcc =\\n    topicAccuracies.length > 0\\n      ? topicAccuracies.reduce((sum, v) => sum + v, 0) / topicAccuracies.length\\n      : null;\\n\\n  const todayPassPct =\\n    reviewsTodayStats.total > 0\\n      ? (reviewsTodayStats.passed / reviewsTodayStats.total) * 100\\n      : null;\\n\\n  let accuracyPct: number;\\n  if (avgQuestionAcc !== null && todayPassPct !== null) {\\n    accuracyPct = avgQuestionAcc * 0.65 + todayPassPct * 0.35;\\n  } else if (avgQuestionAcc !== null) {\\n    accuracyPct = avgQuestionAcc;\\n  } else if (todayPassPct !== null) {\\n    accuracyPct = todayPassPct;\\n  } else {\\n    accuracyPct = 72;\\n  }\\n  accuracyPct = Number(Math.min(100, Math.max(30, accuracyPct)).toFixed(1));\\n\\n  // 2. Infer daily review cadence (cards/day) from today\'s session & recent 7d activity\\n  const sevenDaysAgoMs = now.getTime() - 7 * DAY_MS;\\n  const recentReviewedCount = flashcards.filter(\\n    (fc) => fc.lastReviewedAt && new Date(fc.lastReviewedAt).getTime() >= sevenDaysAgoMs\\n  ).length;\\n\\n  let dailyCadence: number;\\n  let isCadenceEstimated: boolean;\\n  if (reviewsTodayStats.total > 0) {\\n    const recentBaseline = Math.max(4, recentReviewedCount / 2);\\n    dailyCadence = Math.max(\\n      reviewsTodayStats.total,\\n      Number((reviewsTodayStats.total * 0.7 + recentBaseline * 0.3).toFixed(1))\\n    );\\n    isCadenceEstimated = false;\\n  } else if (recentReviewedCount > 0) {\\n    dailyCadence = Math.max(4, Number((recentReviewedCount / 2).toFixed(1)));\\n    isCadenceEstimated = true;\\n  } else {\\n    dailyCadence = 6;\\n    isCadenceEstimated = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  // 3. Evaluate current retention & remaining FSRS consolidation passes per high-incidence card\\n  let retentionSum = 0;\\n  let consolidatedCount = 0;\\n  let basePassesNeeded = 0;\\n\\n  for (const fc of highIncidenceCards) {\\n    const elapsed = computeElapsedDays(fc, now);\\n    const hasFsrsHistory = fc.state !== \'New\' && fc.stability > 0;\\n    const rawTopicAcc = lookupTopicMetric(userAccuracyByTopic, fc);\\n    const normalizedTopicAcc =\\n      rawTopicAcc !== null\\n        ? rawTopicAcc <= 1 && rawTopicAcc >= 0\\n          ? rawTopicAcc * 100\\n          : rawTopicAcc\\n        : accuracyPct;\\n\\n    const cardRetPct = hasFsrsHistory\\n      ? Math.min(99, computeRetrievability(elapsed, fc.stability) * 100)\\n      : Math.min(84, Math.max(45, normalizedTopicAcc * 0.88));\\n\\n    retentionSum += cardRetPct;\\n\\n    // A card is consolidated at the 95% target when in Review with strong stability (>= 12d)\\n    const isConsolidated =\\n      fc.state === \'Review\' && fc.stability >= 12 && cardRetPct >= targetRetentionPct - 2;\\n\\n    if (isConsolidated) {\\n      consolidatedCount += 1;\\n    } else if (fc.state === \'Review\' && fc.stability >= 6) {\\n      basePassesNeeded += 1.2;\\n    } else if (fc.state === \'Review\') {\\n      basePassesNeeded += 2.0;\\n    } else if (fc.state === \'Learning\' || fc.state === \'Relearning\') {\\n      basePassesNeeded += 2.5;\\n    } else {\\n      // New card requires full initial FSRS consolidation sequence\\n      basePassesNeeded += 3.0;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  const currentRetentionPct = Number(\\n    (retentionSum / highIncidenceCards.length).toFixed(1)\\n  );\\n  const retentionGap = Math.max(0, targetRetentionPct - currentRetentionPct);\\n\\n  if (consolidatedCount === highIncidenceCards.length && retentionGap <= 0.5) {\\n    return {\\n      targetRetentionPct,\\n      estimatedDays: 0,\\n      reachedTarget: true,\\n      highIncidenceCount: highIncidenceCards.length,\\n      consolidatedCount,\\n      currentRetentionPct: Math.min(99, currentRetentionPct),\\n      accuracyPct,\\n      dailyCadence,\\n      isCadenceEstimated,\\n      board: selectedBoard,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  // Lower accuracy implies higher lapse rate -> more spaced review passes needed\\n  const accRatio = Math.min(0.98, Math.max(0.4, accuracyPct / 100));\\n  const lapseFrictionMultiplier = 1 + Math.max(0, 0.95 - accRatio) * 1.65;\\n  const totalPassesNeeded = basePassesNeeded * lapseFrictionMultiplier;\\n\\n  // Portion of daily review budget dedicated to high-incidence cards\\n  const highIncidenceShare = highIncidenceCards.length / Math.max(1, flashcards.length);\\n  const effectiveHighIncidenceCadence = Math.max(\\n    1,\\n    dailyCadence * Math.min(1, highIncidenceShare + 0.25)\\n  );\\n\\n  const cadenceDays = totalPassesNeeded / effectiveHighIncidenceCadence;\\n  // Minimum FSRS spacing calendar floor required for long-term stability consolidation\\n  const spacingFloorDays = retentionGap > 0 ? Math.ceil(retentionGap * 0.35) : 1;\\n\\n  const estimatedDays = Math.min(\\n    180,\\n    Math.max(1, Math.round(cadenceDays + spacingFloorDays))\\n  );\\n\\n  return {\\n    targetRetentionPct,\\n    estimatedDays,\\n    reachedTarget: false,\\n    highIncidenceCount: highIncidenceCards.length,\\n    consolidatedCount,\\n    currentRetentionPct,\\n    accuracyPct,\\n    dailyCadence,\\n    isCadenceEstimated,\\n    board: selectedBoard,\\n  };\\n}\", \"StartLine\":645, \"TargetContent\":\"export function getCardCurrentRetrievabilityPct(\\n  card: Flashcard,\\n  now: Date = new Date()\\n): number | null {\\n  if (card.state === \'New\' || card.stability <= 0) return null;\\n  const elapsed = computeElapsedDays(card, now);\\n  return Math.round(computeRetrievability(elapsed, card.stability) * 100);\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/lib/srs.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding retention forecast calculation to srs.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add estimateDaysToTargetRetention in srs.ts\"}"
