  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Unpacking the Request**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on the user\'s specific request. It\'s becoming evident that the ranking display should be encapsulated within a clickable area. The goal is a live ranking, but only revealed when the user interacts, along with a pulsating green indicator and an on/off switch in the sidebar. I\342\200\231m starting to visualize the UI.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Focus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI, specifically the clickable area for the live ranking. It needs to appear solely when the user requests it. I\'m focusing on the implementation details for the clickable sidebar element (that\'s `Sidebar.tsx`, where the ranking control goes) and the corresponding dedicated view, replacing the current, always-visible `<LiveRankingWidget />`. Removing the persistent widget provides a cleaner layout for the question bank, which I\'m taking into consideration as I finalize the placement of elements.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Toggle Element**\n\nI\'m now picturing the details for the retractable sidebar. I\'m focusing on the \"Ranking Ao Vivo\" clickable entry. It will have a pulsating green indicator when active, which is managed via an on/off toggle. I also envision a clean toggle button integrated beside the entry. It will control the pulsing and prevent accidental navigation. The sidebar panel is retractable, using the `PanelLeftClose` / `PanelLeftOpen` toggle. The expanded state will be `lg:w-64`, and compact will be `lg:w-[72px]`.\n\n\n"
